# VS Code REST Client: click Send Request above each call.
# Start: ./run.sh 3
# Automated verification: python3 verify.py --mode 3
# Complete expected bodies: expected/connexion3.json -> withoutNulls (default).
# To include nulls, stop the server and restart: ./run.sh 3 --include-nulls
# Then compare with withNulls and run verify.py --mode 3 --include-nulls.
@baseUrl = http://127.0.0.1:8083/api

### Active versions and adapter: JSONEncoder via Jsonifier, includeNulls=false
# @name c3_runtime
GET {{baseUrl}}/demo/runtime
Accept: application/json

### Model: renamed properties, nested models, datetime/date/Decimal/UUID
# Expected: 200 application/json.
# createdAt="Fri, 05 Apr 2024 06:07:08 GMT".
# birthday="Fri, 05 Apr 2024 00:00:00 GMT", amount="12.50" (string).
# Preserved C3 HTTP dates differ from the strict date-time/date formats.
# note and child.comment are omitted by default.
# Complete body: expected/connexion3.json -> withoutNulls.model
# @name c3_model
GET {{baseUrl}}/demo/model
Accept: application/json

### List: [expected model]
# @name c3_list
GET {{baseUrl}}/demo/list
Accept: application/json

### Dictionary: {"primary": expected model}
# @name c3_map
GET {{baseUrl}}/demo/map
Accept: application/json

### Nulls: false, 0, and "" remain; optionalLabel and child.comment are omitted
# Complete body: expected/connexion3.json -> withoutNulls.nulls
# @name c3_nulls
GET {{baseUrl}}/demo/nulls
Accept: application/json

### OpenAPI document loaded by the generated application
# @name c3_openapi
GET {{baseUrl}}/openapi.json
Accept: application/json

### Swagger UI: expected 200 text/html; open the URL in a browser to interact
GET {{baseUrl}}/ui/
